      "mergeID": "5eab5da5d21f8857cfd3e37c",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I'm coming from Unreal Engine 4's blueprints system to Udon, and while it's amazing, and feature-rich, there's one main thing that throws me off while Udon graphing that I think could be an easy fix. In blueprinting, if no blocks are selected and you right click on an empty part of the graph editor, it brings up a search bar on your mouse location that lets you search for blocks and when you add a block it adds it at the location of your cursor, rather than at 0,0. I think adding that as an option for Udon graphing would make programming in Udon much, much faster.",
